<body>
  <main>
    <header>
      <h1>Ace-Step 1.5 Diffusers Implementation Guide</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A SynthaEngine research guide for adding Ace-Step 1.5 as an audio/music
        workflow family through Diffusers <code>AceStepPipeline</code>, with
        local hardware feasibility notes for 64 GB RAM and RTX 3060 12 GB VRAM.
      </p>
      <div class="meta">
        <span class="pill">Date: 2026-05-30</span>
        <span class="pill">Target PC: 64 GB RAM, RTX 3060 12 GB</span>
        <span class="pill">Diffusers: 0.38.0 verified locally</span>
        <span class="pill">Initial task: ace-step.text2music</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="toc">
      <h2 id="toc">Contents</h2>
      <nav class="toc">
        <a href="#summary">1. Executive Summary</a>
        <a href="#what">2. What This Is</a>
        <a href="#modalities">3. Modalities and Sub-Pipelines</a>
        <a href="#variants">4. Model Variants</a>
        <a href="#hardware">5. Hardware Feasibility</a>
        <a href="#quantization">6. Quantization</a>
        <a href="#hosting">7. Cloud and Hosting</a>
        <a href="#smoke">8. Smoke Test</a>
        <a href="#implementation">9. SynthaEngine Plan</a>
        <a href="#options">10. Options and Flags</a>
        <a href="#done">11. Definition of Done</a>
        <a href="#sources">12. Sources</a>
      </nav>
    </section>

    <section id="summary">
      <h2>1. Executive Summary</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card ok">
          <strong>Pipeline exists locally</strong>
          <p>
            The repo venv imports <code>AceStepPipeline</code>,
            <code>AceStepTransformer1DModel</code>, and
            <code>AutoencoderOobleck</code> with Diffusers 0.38.0.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card ok">
          <strong>RTX 3060 is viable for 2B</strong>
          <p>
            Start with the 2B turbo path, short durations, one job at a time,
            BF16, and model CPU offload.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card warn">
          <strong>Audio support is required</strong>
          <p>
            SynthaEngine needs audio artifacts, audio outputs, history playback,
            and a subprocess-backed <code>backend/ace_step</code> runtime.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p>
        Ace-Step 1.5 is an audio/music model, not an image or video model. The
        safest first integration is <code>ace-step.text2music</code> only.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="what">
      <h2>2. What This Is</h2>
      <p>
        Ace-Step 1.5 is an open-source music generation foundation model. It
        generates variable-length stereo audio at 48 kHz from text prompts and
        optional structured lyrics. The full upstream system combines a
        language-model planner with a Diffusion Transformer synthesizer, while
        Diffusers exposes the DiT/audio synthesis side through
        <code>AceStepPipeline</code>.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Component</th><th>Role</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>AceStepPipeline</code></td><td>Diffusers pipeline for music generation and audio editing tasks.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>AutoencoderOobleck</code></td><td>Audio VAE for waveform to/from stereo latents.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>AceStepTransformer1DModel</code></td><td>Diffusion Transformer denoiser in audio latent space.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Qwen3-based text encoder</td><td>Prompt and lyric conditioning.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>AceStepConditionEncoder</code></td><td>Combines text, lyric, and timbre conditioning.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>FlowMatchEulerDiscreteScheduler</code></td><td>Flow-matching sampling schedule.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section id="modalities">
      <h2>3. Modalities and Sub-Pipelines</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Task type</th><th>What it does</th><th>Initial status</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>text2music</code></td><td>Generate music from prompts and lyrics.</td><td>Implement first.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>cover</code></td><td>Generate audio with timbre transfer from reference audio or semantic codes.</td><td>Later.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>repaint</code></td><td>Regenerate a region of existing audio.</td><td>Later.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>extract</code></td><td>Extract a track such as vocals or drums.</td><td>Later.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>lego</code></td><td>Generate a specific track from audio context.</td><td>Later.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>complete</code></td><td>Complete audio with additional track classes.</td><td>Later.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        Inputs can include text, lyrics, source audio, reference audio, semantic
        audio codes, track names, and music metadata such as BPM, key, and time
        signature. Outputs should be persisted as WAV files in SynthaEngine.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="variants">
      <h2>4. Model Variants</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Variant</th><th>Hub repo</th><th>CFG</th><th>Default steps</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>turbo</td><td><code>ACE-Step/Ace-Step1.5</code></td><td>off, distilled</td><td>8</td><td>Best first local target.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>base</td><td><code>ACE-Step/acestep-v15-base</code></td><td>on</td><td>8 documented; often 30-60 for quality</td><td>More tunable.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>sft</td><td><code>ACE-Step/acestep-v15-sft</code></td><td>on</td><td>8 documented; often 30-60 for quality</td><td>Higher quality, narrower behavior.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>XL Turbo</td><td><code>ACE-Step/acestep-v15-xl-turbo-diffusers</code></td><td>off, distilled</td><td>8</td><td>Advanced only; use offload plus INT8 on 12 GB.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section id="hardware">
      <h2>5. Hardware Feasibility</h2>
      <p>
        Local facts: CUDA and BF16 are available on the RTX 3060 12 GB;
        <code>bitsandbytes</code>, <code>scipy</code>, and
        <code>torchaudio</code> are installed; <code>torchao</code>,
        <code>optimum-quanto</code>, <code>flash_attn</code>, and
        <code>soundfile</code> are not installed.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Option</th><th>Feasible?</th><th>Recommendation</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>2B turbo, 10-30 sec, BF16, one job</td><td>Yes</td><td>First target.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2B turbo with model CPU offload</td><td>Yes</td><td>Recommended app default.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2B direct CUDA</td><td>Probably, measure first</td><td>Smoke test only before exposing.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Base/SFT, 30-60 steps</td><td>Yes, slower</td><td>Advanced quality mode.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Long 5-10 minute generation</td><td>No by default</td><td>Stress-test later.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Batching multiple songs</td><td>No by default</td><td>Serialize jobs instead.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>XL Turbo on 12 GB</td><td>Yes with caution</td><td>Require offload plus INT8 experiment.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>XL direct CUDA</td><td>No</td><td>Use larger GPU.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <h3>Recommended Defaults</h3>
      <pre><code>{
  "model": "ACE-Step1.5 Turbo",
  "variant": "turbo",
  "audio_duration": 30.0,
  "num_inference_steps": 8,
  "guidance_scale": 1.0,
  "shift": 3.0,
  "num_audios": 1,
  "vocal_language": "en",
  "memory_preset": "model_offload",
  "quantization": "none",
  "output_format": "wav"
}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section id="quantization">
      <h2>6. Quantization</h2>
      <p>
        SynthaEngine already has a Diffusers pipeline quantization helper for
        <code>none</code> and <code>bnb_8bit</code>. Treat
        <code>bnb_8bit</code> as the first advanced experiment for Ace-Step,
        especially for XL. Keep BF16 as the initial default for 2B turbo.
      </p>
      <pre><code>from backend.quantization import build_diffusers_pipeline_quantization_config

quantization_config = build_diffusers_pipeline_quantization_config(
    "bnb_8bit",
    components_to_quantize=["transformer", "text_encoder"],
    task_type="ace-step.text2music",
)</code></pre>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Mode</th><th>Expose initially?</th><th>Reason</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>BF16 / <code>none</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Stable first path.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>bnb_8bit</code></td><td>Advanced after smoke test</td><td>Installed locally and already patterned in the app.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>bnb_4bit</code></td><td>No</td><td>Needs new helper branch and quality validation.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>torchao</td><td>No</td><td>Not installed.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Quanto</td><td>No</td><td>Not installed.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>GGUF</td><td>No</td><td>Separate C++ runner, not Diffusers.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section id="hosting">
      <h2>7. Cloud and Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The checked official ACE-Step model cards do not show an active Hugging
        Face Inference Provider deployment. Treat cloud as GPU hosting for your
        runtime rather than a guaranteed managed model API.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Provider</th><th>Useful GPUs</th><th>Best use</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Hugging Face Spaces GPU</td><td>L4 24 GB, A10G 24 GB, L40S 48 GB, A100 80 GB</td><td>Demos close to Hub models.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>RunPod</td><td>RTX 3090/4090 24 GB, A40/L40S 48 GB, A100/H100 80 GB</td><td>Flexible pods/serverless experiments.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Lambda GPU Cloud</td><td>A10 24 GB, A6000 48 GB, A100/H100 classes when available</td><td>Managed VM development.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section id="smoke">
      <h2>8. Smoke Test</h2>
      <p>
        Before integration, run one standalone 20-30 second turbo generation and
        write a WAV with <code>scipy</code>, which is already available locally.
      </p>
      <pre><code>from pathlib import Path

import numpy as np
import torch
from diffusers import AceStepPipeline
from scipy.io import wavfile

pipe = AceStepPipeline.from_pretrained(
    "ACE-Step/Ace-Step1.5",
    torch_dtype=torch.bfloat16,
)
pipe.enable_model_cpu_offload()

if getattr(pipe, "vae", None) is not None and hasattr(pipe.vae, "enable_tiling"):
    pipe.vae.enable_tiling()

output = pipe(
    prompt="An upbeat synthwave track with driving drums and warm analog bass",
    lyrics="[verse]\nNeon lights are calling\n[chorus]\nWe ride the wave tonight",
    audio_duration=20.0,
    vocal_language="en",
    num_inference_steps=8,
    guidance_scale=1.0,
    shift=3.0,
    generator=torch.Generator(device="cpu").manual_seed(42),
)

audio = output.audios[0].detach().cpu().float()
audio_np = audio.T.numpy() if audio.ndim == 2 else audio.numpy()
audio_np = np.clip(audio_np, -1.0, 1.0)
wavfile.write(Path("ace_step_smoke.wav"), int(pipe.sample_rate), (audio_np * 32767).astype(np.int16))</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section id="implementation">
      <h2>9. SynthaEngine Plan</h2>
      <h3>Public Identifiers</h3>
      <pre><code>family: ace-step
first task: ace-step.text2music
later tasks:
  ace-step.cover
  ace-step.repaint
  ace-step.extract
  ace-step.lego
  ace-step.complete</code></pre>

      <h3>Required Capability Additions</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Audio upload/artifact support with a new audio artifact prefix.</li>
        <li><code>AudiosWithBatchOutput</code> returning <code>batch_id</code> and <code>audios</code>.</li>
        <li>History and frontend audio playback.</li>
        <li><code>backend/ace_step/</code> subprocess runtime using <code>AceStepPipeline</code>.</li>
        <li>Explicit WAV writing and JSON sidecar metadata.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Initial Schema Sketch</h3>
      <pre><code>class AceStepText2MusicInputs(BaseModel):
    prompt: str = ""
    lyrics: str = ""
    audio_duration: float = Field(default=30.0, ge=10.0, le=120.0)
    vocal_language: str = "en"
    steps: int = Field(default=8, ge=1, le=100)
    guidance_scale: float = Field(default=1.0, ge=0.0, le=30.0)
    shift: float = Field(default=3.0, ge=1.0, le=3.0)
    seed: int | None = None
    model: str | None = None
    variant: Literal["turbo", "base", "sft", "xl_turbo"] = "turbo"
    num_audios: int = Field(default=1, ge=1, le=1)
    bpm: int | None = Field(default=None, ge=40, le=240)
    keyscale: str | None = None
    timesignature: str | None = None
    instruction: str | None = None
    max_text_length: int = Field(default=256, ge=32, le=512)
    max_lyric_length: int = Field(default=2048, ge=0, le=4096)
    cfg_interval_start: float = Field(default=0.0, ge=0.0, le=1.0)
    cfg_interval_end: float = Field(default=1.0, ge=0.0, le=1.0)
    output_format: Literal["wav"] = "wav"
    memory_preset: Literal["direct_cuda", "model_offload", "sequential_offload"] = "model_offload"
    quantization: Literal["none", "bnb_8bit"] = "none"
    experimental_ack: bool = True</code></pre>

      <h3>Runtime Sketch</h3>
      <pre><code>@torch.inference_mode()
def generate_text2music_in_process(params: dict[str, object]) -> dict[str, object]:
    pipe = None
    try:
        pipe = load_ace_step_pipeline(
            model=params.get("model"),
            variant=str(params.get("variant") or "turbo"),
            memory_preset=str(params.get("memory_preset") or "model_offload"),
            quantization=str(params.get("quantization") or "none"),
        )

        output = pipe(
            prompt=str(params.get("prompt") or ""),
            lyrics=str(params.get("lyrics") or ""),
            audio_duration=float(params.get("audio_duration") or 30.0),
            vocal_language=str(params.get("vocal_language") or "en"),
            num_inference_steps=int(params.get("steps") or 8),
            guidance_scale=float(params.get("guidance_scale") or 1.0),
            shift=float(params.get("shift") or 3.0),
            generator=torch.Generator(device="cpu").manual_seed(resolve_seed(params.get("seed"))),
            task_type="text2music",
        )
        return save_audio_output(output.audios[0], sample_rate=pipe.sample_rate, params=params)
    finally:
        release_pipeline(pipe, logger=logger)</code></pre>

      <h3>Workflow Example</h3>
      <pre><code>{
  "kind": "workflow",
  "payload": {
    "tasks": [
      {
        "id": "t1",
        "type": "ace-step.text2music",
        "inputs": {
          "prompt": "upbeat synthwave track with driving drums and warm analog bass",
          "lyrics": "[verse]\nNeon lights are calling\n[chorus]\nWe ride the wave tonight",
          "audio_duration": 30.0,
          "vocal_language": "en",
          "steps": 8,
          "guidance_scale": 1.0,
          "shift": 3.0,
          "memory_preset": "model_offload",
          "quantization": "none",
          "experimental_ack": true
        }
      }
    ],
    "return": "@t1.audios"
  }
}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section id="options">
      <h2>10. Options and Flags</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Option</th><th>Expose initially?</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>prompt</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Music description.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>lyrics</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Structured sections such as verse/chorus.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>audio_duration</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Default 30 sec, cap initially.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>vocal_language</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Should match lyrics.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>num_inference_steps</code></td><td>Yes as steps</td><td>Turbo default 8.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>guidance_scale</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Turbo ignores CFG guidance above 1.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>shift</code></td><td>Advanced</td><td>Default 3.0.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>seed/generator</code></td><td>Yes as seed</td><td>Use CPU generator.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>instruction</code></td><td>Advanced</td><td>Auto-generated when omitted.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>max_text_length</code>, <code>max_lyric_length</code></td><td>Advanced</td><td>Prompt and lyric token caps.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>bpm</code>, <code>keyscale</code>, <code>timesignature</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Optional music metadata controls.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>task_type</code></td><td>No free text</td><td>Map to workflow task ids.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>track_name</code>, <code>complete_track_classes</code></td><td>Later</td><td>Track tasks.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>src_audio</code>, <code>reference_audio</code></td><td>Later</td><td>Requires audio artifact support.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>audio_codes</code></td><td>Later</td><td>Semantic-code cover path.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>repainting_start</code>, <code>repainting_end</code></td><td>Later</td><td>Repaint/lego.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>audio_cover_strength</code></td><td>Later</td><td>Cover blending.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>cfg_interval_start</code>, <code>cfg_interval_end</code></td><td>Advanced</td><td>Validate start <= end.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>timesteps</code>, callbacks, latents</td><td>No</td><td>Internal or future advanced controls.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section id="done">
      <h2>11. Definition of Done</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Audio artifacts can be uploaded and cleaned up.</li>
        <li><code>ace-step.text2music</code> appears in workflow task discovery.</li>
        <li>The catalog exposes an <code>ace-step</code> audio capability.</li>
        <li>Workflow jobs return <code>audios</code> URLs.</li>
        <li>WAV files and sidecar metadata are written under <code>outputs/batch_*</code>.</li>
        <li>History can show and play audio records.</li>
        <li>Runtime is subprocess-backed, serialized, and cleans up pipeline hooks.</li>
        <li>Tests cover schemas, catalog, adapter dispatch, subprocess bridge, and history without downloading the model.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="sources">
      <h2>12. Sources</h2>
